# Rental Admin

Follow the root `CLAUDE.md` as the source of truth. Do not invent a parallel stack.

Hard rules:

- pnpm monorepo: `apps/web` (Next.js App Router), `apps/api` (Express), `packages/shared`.
- No React Router. No second QueryClient. No extra UI kit or HTTP client.
- Feature UI: `features/<name>/{api,hooks,schemas,components}`. Pages stay thin.
- Components call hooks; hooks call `*-api.ts`; only `apiClient` / `storageClient` talk to the network.
- Query keys only from `lib/query-keys.ts`. Invalidate `files.all` / `dashboard.all` after mutations.
- API pipeline: `route → validateRequest(Zod) → controller → service → Prisma|S3`. Thin controllers.
- Direct-to-S3 uploads. Never send `storageKey` or AWS secrets to the browser.
- Shared contracts in `@rental-admin/shared`. Build `shared` before web/api.
- TypeScript strict, kebab-case files, named component exports, English UI copy.
- Conventional commits (`feat(files): …`). Do not commit `.env` or credentials.
